  clock: 2  # 94b7
  nonce: 94b7  # 94b7
  message: "Tier 2 verification (post-ADR-0027/0028 closure): the L3 producer-coherence and L4 fallback-coherence linters that landed in the [Unreleased] cycle enforce emit-site conformance (consumers must use canonical registry values), NOT dataclass field introduction. WI-busij's scope — pre-commit detection when a new multi-value field is added to ir.py/datamodels.py without an axis-declaration ADR — remains distinct and unbuilt. Trigger condition (c) from this item's 'When to land' section ('ADR-0027/ADR-0028/a future axis ADR ships with new multi-value fields') has now fired twice without WI-busij landing, but no drift has escaped (the registries+drift linters caught what they were supposed to catch). So the preventive-automation argument is not strengthened by recent history. Recommend leaving as-is; pick up if/when an actual incident surfaces."  # 94b7
